 is a medical condition characterized by the heart's inability to pump blood sufficiently to meet the body's needs. This condition often leads to fluid retention and various complications. It is commonly associated with heart disease and may necessitate adjustments in fluid and nutrient administration, particularly in the context of parenteral nutrition for children.\",7\r\n15087,HIPO-NATREMIA,\"Hipo-natremia refers to a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, which can be caused by various factors including fluid imbalance and hormonal issues.\",10\r\n15069,HIPONATREMIA EUVOLÉMICA,\"Hiponatremia euvolémica es una condición médica que se presenta en pacientes que reciben nutrición artificial. Se caracteriza por niveles bajos de sodio en la sangre, pero sin una disminución del volumen de líquido corporal. En este tipo de hiponatremia, el volumen sanguíneo se mantiene normal, lo que distingue a esta condición de otras formas de hiponatremia que pueden estar asociadas con una reducción del volumen de líquido.\",9\r\n5657,FUROSEMIDA,\"Furosemida, also known as furosemide, is a diuretic medication primarily used to treat fluid build-up associated with conditions such as heart failure, liver scarring, and kidney disease. It is effective in managing fluid retention and high blood pressure, and it can also assist in the treatment of hypercalcemia and hyponatremia by promoting the elimination of excess water from the body. \n\nTo maximize its effectiveness, furosemida should be taken on an empty stomach, as food can alter gastrointestinal motility and reduce its bioavailability. Additionally, it is often used in conjunction with other treatments for conditions like the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). Overall, furosemida plays a crucial role in managing fluid balance and sodium levels in patients with various medical conditions.\",6\r\n5594,FLUDROCORTISONA,\"Fludrocortisona, also known as fludrocortisone, is a synthetic corticosteroid medication primarily used in the treatment of isolated aldosterone deficiency and adrenal insufficiency. It plays a crucial role in managing conditions related to insufficient production of aldosterone, helping to regulate sodium and potassium levels in the body.\",2\r\n15077,FURST FORMULA,\"The Furst formula is a calculation utilized in the medical field to estimate renal capacity for eliminating free water, particularly in patients diagnosed with Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). Additionally, it serves as a method for calculating sodium and potassium levels in patients experiencing hyponatremia. This dual application highlights the formula's importance in managing electrolyte imbalances and assessing renal function in specific clinical scenarios.\",2\r\n5235,INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL AGUDA,\"Acute adrenal insufficiency is a medical emergency characterized by low blood pressure and volume depletion, requiring immediate treatment.\",8\r\n4009,POLIDIPSIA PRIMARIA,\"Polidipsia primaria es un trastorno que se caracteriza por la sed excesiva y la ingesta de grandes cantidades de agua. Esta condición puede resultar en una dilución de la orina, lo que implica que el cuerpo está consumiendo más líquidos de lo que necesita, afectando así el equilibrio hídrico del organismo.\",2\r\n5593,ZARZUELO A,Zarzuelo A is an author who contributed to the book on pharmacological interactions.,1\r\n15088,HIPO-NATREMIA HIPOVOLÉMICA,\"Hypo-natremia hypovolemic is a specific type of hyponatremia caused by a decrease in blood volume, often due to fluid loss.\",1\r\n15089,HIPO-NATREMIA HIPERVOLEMICA,\"Hypo-natremia hypervolemic is a type of hyponatremia that occurs when there is an excess of fluid in the body, diluting sodium levels.\",1\r\n15073,FURST,\"La fórmula de Furst es un cálculo utilizado para estimar la capacidad renal de eliminar agua libre, relevante en el manejo de la hiponatremia.\",1\r\n15074,INTOXICACIÓN AGUDA DE AGUA,\"La intoxicac